50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are Microbiome Atlas, Plant Drought Signaling, Protein Folding Dynamics, and Regeneration in Amphibians.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I think we should consider the Microbiome Atlas project, as it seems to have a broad impact.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree, but we should also consider the Plant Drought Signaling research, given the current climate concerns.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, I think the Protein Folding Dynamics study has more immediate applications in medicine.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, I think the Regeneration in Amphibians investigation could lead to breakthroughs in regenerative medicine.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, that's a valid point, but we should also consider the feasibility and timeline of each project.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, the Microbiome Atlas has a clear plan and timeline, and it builds on existing infrastructure.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the Plant Drought Signaling research also has a well-defined scope and could provide quick results.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the Protein Folding Dynamics study has a higher risk, but also a higher potential reward.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the Regeneration in Amphibians investigation is risky, but it could lead to groundbreaking discoveries.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, I think we should also consider the availability of resources and personnel for each project.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, the Microbiome Atlas has a large team and access to many field sites.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the Plant Drought Signaling research has a smaller team, but they have experience with greenhouse trials.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the Protein Folding Dynamics study requires specialized equipment and expertise.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the Regeneration in Amphibians investigation needs access to specific animal models and facilities.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
